   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The feeling comes to you",
     "texto": [
      "In Spanish, you do not «do» many feelings: they **come to you**. What causes them is the **subject**, and you are **me**, **te**, **le**, **nos**, **os** or **les**.\n\n- **Me da vergüenza** hablar en público.\n- **Me pone nerviosa** la entrevista. The adjective agrees with the person who feels.\n- **Me alegra**, **me molesta**, **me preocupa** + infinitive or noun.\n\nIf what causes the feeling is plural, so is the verb: **me molestan** los ruidos.\n\nWhen the subject changes you use **que** + subjunctive: **Me alegra que vengas**. For now the infinitive is enough."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Three ways to say what you feel",
     "texto": [
      "There are three very common structures:\n\n- **dar** + feeling: **me da** vergüenza, miedo, pena, rabia, risa.\n- **poner** + adjective: **me pone** nervioso, triste, contento.\n- a feeling verb: **me alegra**, **me molesta**, **me preocupa**, **me aburre**, **me sorprende**.\n\nIn all three, what causes the feeling is the **subject**: an action in the infinitive or a thing. If it is plural, the verb is plural: **me ponen nervioso** los exámenes."
     ],
